{"event_type":"review","id":"a20aead89fceb308cae7e9bce36880752021d3b8d6510d6d58008af1a034a16a","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T17:07:10Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/0b3c37872b8b201f6e8ba25c54561db9ea16aa3548413aae71b9d870d64cb9a9","sha256":"0b3c37872b8b201f6e8ba25c54561db9ea16aa3548413aae71b9d870d64cb9a9"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/7f5b83952029ffc42f1e9f2dc6c7af78eb2e2c1a4e05865ea85370cd04a22b9c","sha256":"7f5b83952029ffc42f1e9f2dc6c7af78eb2e2c1a4e05865ea85370cd04a22b9c"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/24fdf89bd28b8f989bb6a04dcc7ed9334dac5921f8bd2272f18d3dd048af0f5c","sha256":"24fdf89bd28b8f989bb6a04dcc7ed9334dac5921f8bd2272f18d3dd048af0f5c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/af88161e1b025f71437b85caa12d843ed01e0cf51b9087a329c9d534cdb5e0dd","sha256":"af88161e1b025f71437b85caa12d843ed01e0cf51b9087a329c9d534cdb5e0dd"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5a344f752600c55282bdea67f91f851841bbafb0914b866c89736e82b7047400","sha256":"5a344f752600c55282bdea67f91f851841bbafb0914b866c89736e82b7047400"}],"attempt_id":"259dd25db5dfcb76e03c9bcde507caa44229bedfdab679f133e4b728a4e719b7:0:1","base":"d46948ae2e47cde42ce5041720fa1ddc025c0658","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"8e4171161f5a3983a37d2ea46490eb4daf86fe2d","body":"**The prompt-cap comment is stale.**\n\nLine 12 says \"4 tools\". The baseline sets `maxTools: 6` at Line 189. Update the comment to match.\n\n```diff\n-//   - modest prompt caps (4 tools, 20k-char system prompt, 1k-char per-tool\n+//   - modest prompt caps (6 tools, 20k-char system prompt, 1k-char per-tool\n```","id":"c184569bfd1531afab4a53eab4779174fe32fc40422065fcb12ea016601d5e6b","intervals":[],"path":"src/harness/config.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"The prompt-cap comment is stale."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"aea0e3eef00f31a677d31c0f1aac18997071012f","body":"**Update `harness-live.test.ts`, which still imports `SubprocessDriver` from the root barrel.**\n\nThe live conformance leg loads `dist/index.js` and destructures `SubprocessDriver` from it. This change removes that export from `src/index.ts`, so the value is `undefined`. The leg then fails at `new SubprocessDriver(...)` when `CQ_LIVE_CLI=1` is set. The `LiveDriverModule` cast hides the missing export from the typechecker, so the failure appears only at runtime.\n\nThe leg is opt-in, and CI does not run it. Rebind the test to the merged `ClaudeCodeDriver` surface. Confirm that its constructor options match the calls in this file, and confirm that `SessionStore` and `defaultHarnessConfig` are still exported from the barrel. The inspected evidence does not establish a safe replacement binding, so this comment does not include a code edit.","id":"78426e0764829428eb549c522c031fbdccc1fb5acad50b746009912d9cf0eac7","intervals":[],"path":"src/index.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Update `harness-live.test.ts`, which still imports `SubprocessDriver` from the root barrel."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"74a199bba441aa1504df9fa3584913158f94d597","body":"**Reject requested-ID collisions before appending.**\n\n`SessionStore.create` is public and accepts any filesystem-safe ID, including one already returned by `create`. A collision appends a second header, and `load` then rejects the record with `duplicate header`.\n\nUse an exclusive initial write:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     await appendFile(this.pathFor(sessionId), `${JSON.stringify(line)}\\n`, {\n       encoding: 'utf8',\n       mode: 0o600,\n+      flag: 'wx',\n     });\n```\n\n</details>\n\nIf callers must recreate empty or torn records, handle `EEXIST` explicitly. Keep the error for non-empty records.","id":"f0014312b2f61ef41c4f6b461be0fee231527ada42bcc5dbc00e5d45c5341c4c","intervals":[],"path":"src/harness/session.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject requested-ID collisions before appending."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"b059d51882b91b91cbff88d646435c9ef2a3e1f9","body":"**Coerce decimal spellings at numeric schema fields.**\n\n`parseFlags` keeps `2.50` as a string. `run-plan` and generated plan commands then pass that string to `z.number()` fields, so common decimal spellings can fail input validation. The numeric-schema test does not establish a rejection contract because it passes an unused schema argument to the one-argument `parseFlags` function.\n\nKeep identifier protection in `parseFlags`, but convert decimal-only strings at these numeric fields:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n+const decimalFlag = (value: unknown): unknown =>\n+  typeof value === 'string' && /^(?:\\d+|\\d*\\.\\d+)$/.test(value) ? Number(value) : value;\n+\n-    concurrency: z.number().int().min(1).default(4),\n+    concurrency: z.preprocess(decimalFlag, z.number().int().min(1)).default(4),\n...\n-    maxUsd: z.number().min(0).optional(),\n+    maxUsd: z.preprocess(decimalFlag, z.number().min(0)).optional(),\n...\n-    maxTokens: z.number().int().positive().optional(),\n+    maxTokens: z.preprocess(decimalFlag, z.number().int().positive()).optional(),\n```\n\n</details>","id":"8a83dc121be274eea3e7606111b0b55e0bbc57313b2b421d205979ee4f820ed5","intervals":[],"path":"src/cli/main.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Coerce decimal spellings at numeric schema fields."}],"head":"90885f6131963a135a326aa8362610a922725eb3","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"cfcf0a047f2947a0486047f5b7f5dda12c199270","intervals":[[5,5],[8,26],[28,40],[44,48],[52,59],[65,66]],"path":"src/cli/README.md"},{"blob":"b05